- The Jacobian is exactly `1-3^{2m}x^{4m}` over `Q[x]`, not a congruence. Clean next-digit representatives are well-defined even when `3|(2k+1)`.
- Same-residue lifts at cap `D=2m+1` have residual `-x^{4m}+U_x+V_y`; mixed monomials, Frobenius, shears, representative changes, and the quadratic term cannot cancel `x^{4m}`.
- `m=3` recovers the frozen D7 point and the clean `1566` coefficient. `m=5` gives the D11 point modulo `3^{10}=59049`:
